@event between_circling
# en: Circling
title [bfe19a] = 兜圈子
# en: {~{a} and {b} have sat next to each other at three lectures running, by accident, all three times on purpose.|{a} asks you, very casually, whether {b} is seeing anyone. Ten minutes later {b} asks you the same about {a}.|{a} and {b} keep arriving at the same doorway at the same moment, and then insisting the other goes first, for some time.} Everyone can see it except, apparently, the two of them.
text [dc179e] = {~{a}和{b}已经连着三节课坐在一起了，每次都是“碰巧”，每次都是故意的。|{a}很随意地问你，{b}有没有在跟谁交往。十分钟后，{b}也来问你{a}的事。|{a}和{b}总是同时走到同一扇门口，然后互相谦让，让对方先走，让了好半天。}所有人都看得出来，除了他们俩自己。
# en: Two students reaching for the same door handle at the same moment, both pulling back, a third watching from the stairs with a hand over their eyes.
scene [438ec9] = 两个学生同时伸手去拉同一个门把手，又同时缩回手；第三个人在楼梯上看着，一只手捂住了眼睛。
# en: Give them a push
opt.left.label [0b2807] = 推他们一把
# en: {~You make sure the only free seat at the next lecture is the one beside {b}, and that {a} knows it. They walk out together.|You tell {a} that {b} asked. You tell {b} that {a} asked. Both of these things are true. That evening they're on the same bench.|You hold the door yourself and wave them both through at once. They collide, apologise, and laugh, and keep laughing all the way down the corridor.}
opt.left.say.1 [b90cbf] = {~你确保下节课唯一的空位就在{b}旁边，还让{a}知道了这一点。下课时，他们是一起走出去的。|你对{a}说，{b}问起过。你对{b}说，{a}也问起过。这两件事都是真的。当天晚上，他们坐在了同一条长凳上。|你亲自扶着门，挥手让他们俩同时进去。两人撞了个满怀，连声道歉，然后笑了起来，一路笑到走廊尽头。}
# en: {~Your hint lands like a brick. {a} goes scarlet and sits at the far end of the hall for a week.|{b} asks you, coolly, what exactly you meant by that. You don't have a good answer.|You arrange it all perfectly and both of them see straight through it. They're mortified, and a little annoyed with you, separately.}
opt.left.say.2 [f3a1b5] = {~你的暗示像块砖头一样砸了下去。{a}的脸涨得通红，接下来一个星期都坐在大厅的另一头。|{b}冷冷地问你，那话到底是什么意思。你答不上来。|你安排得天衣无缝，两人却都一眼看穿了。他们羞得无地自容，还各自对你有点恼火。}
# en: Leave them to it
opt.right.label [4dcfa4] = 随他们去
# en: {~You keep your nose in your book. A month on they're still sitting together by accident.|You say nothing. {a} looks at you as if hoping you would.|You leave them to it. They hold the door for each other for the rest of the term.}
opt.right.say.1 [26f5e2] = {~你埋头看书。一个月后，他们还在“碰巧”坐在一起。|你什么也没说。{a}看着你，好像盼着你说点什么。|你随他们去了。整个学期，他们都在互相给对方扶门。}

@event between_love_note
# en: Sealed With Wax
title [6e60f3] = 蜡封的纸条
# en: {a} presses a folded note into your hand, sealed with candle wax and, by the look of it, a great deal of worry. "For {b}. Don't read it. Don't let {b.them} open it in front of anyone. Don't say it's from me." You point out that {b} will know who it's from. {a} looks stricken.
text [6ba3a2] = {a}把一张折好的纸条塞进你手里，用烛蜡封着，看样子还封进了满满的忐忑。“给{b}的。别看。别让{b.them}当着别人的面拆。别说是我写的。”你指出，{b}会知道是谁写的。{a}一脸惊恐。
# en: A student pressing a folded note sealed with a blob of candle wax into a friend's hand, looking over their shoulder.
scene [e51b6c] = 一个学生把一张用烛蜡封好的折叠纸条塞进朋友手里，一边回头张望。
# en: Deliver it as asked
opt.left.label [710169] = 照吩咐送去
# en: You give up the evening you'd meant for your essay, find {b} alone in the library, and hand it over. {b} reads it twice, goes pink to the ears, and asks you, with great dignity, to tell {a} "yes. Probably. Thursday."
opt.left.say.1 [d65912] = 你推掉了原本留给论文的那个晚上，在图书馆找到独自一人的{b}，把纸条递了过去。{b}读了两遍，红到了耳根，然后非常庄重地请你转告{a}：“好。大概吧。星期四。”
# en: {b} reads it in the library and goes quiet. "Tell {a} it's very kind," {b.they} say{b.s}, which is the worst thing anyone can say. You carry it back as gently as you can.
opt.left.say.2 [470daa] = {b}在图书馆里读完纸条，沉默了。“告诉{a}，这真的很贴心，”{b.they}说——这是世上最糟的一句话。你尽可能温柔地把它带了回去。
# en: Help {a} write it better
opt.right.label [4738eb] = 帮{a}把它写得更好
# en: You sit up with {a} over four drafts, crossing out the poetry. What's left is three plain lines, the best thing {a} has ever written, and {b} answers them the same evening. You find out how it went at breakfast, from the way they arrive together.
opt.right.say.1 [07d52e] = 你陪{a}熬夜改了四稿，把诗句统统划掉。剩下的是三行朴素的话，是{a}写过的最好的东西，{b}当天傍晚就回了信。第二天早饭时，看他们俩一起走进来的样子，你就知道结果了。
# en: By the fourth draft it's a sonnet, and a bad one, and {a} has gone off the whole idea. "I'll just tell {b.them}. One day." The note stays in {their} pocket for the rest of the term. You can see the corner of it.
opt.right.say.2 [0ddcd4] = 改到第四稿，它成了一首十四行诗，还是首蹩脚的，{a}也彻底没了兴致。“我还是直接告诉{b.them}吧。总有一天。”整个学期，那张纸条都待在{their}口袋里。你看得见露出来的那个角。

@event between_find_out
# en: Asking for a Friend
title [7efb36] = 替朋友问问
# en: "You know {b}," says {a}, in a library whisper that carries for three shelves. "Could you find out if {b.they} ever, you know. Thinks about me. At all. Without saying I asked." {a} adds, after a moment, "Especially without saying I asked."
text [77faab] = “你认识{b}，”{a}用图书馆式的耳语说，声音却传出了三排书架。“你能不能打听一下，{b.they}有没有，你懂的，想过我。哪怕一点点。别说是我问的。”过了一会儿，{a}又补充道：“尤其别说是我问的。”
# en: A student whispering urgently to a friend in a library alcove, both of them looking across the room at a third student who hasn't noticed.
scene [e805d5] = 图书馆的壁龛里，一个学生急切地对朋友耳语，两人都望着房间另一头一个毫无察觉的学生。
# en: Ask {b} straight out
opt.left.label [b91ef8] = 直接去问{b}
# en: {b} looks at you for a long moment, then laughs. "Did {a} put you up to this? Tell {a} the answer's yes, and that {a} can ask me {a.them}self next time."
opt.left.say.1 [a5db32] = {b}看了你好一会儿，然后笑了。“是{a}让你来的吧？告诉{a}，答案是‘是’，下次让{a}自己来问。”
# en: {b} is kind about it, which makes it harder. "I like {a}. Just not like that." You carry it back, and {a} says "right, of course", and talks about the weather for some time.
opt.left.say.2 [985aee] = {b}回答得很体贴，这反而更难受。“我喜欢{a}。只是不是那种喜欢。”你把话带了回去，{a}说“好吧，当然”，然后聊了很久的天气。
# en: Find out sideways
opt.right.label [80b8e5] = 旁敲侧击
# en: Three casual questions, one about the Midwinter Ball, and you have your answer: {b} goes slightly pink at {a}'s name. You report back. {a} has to sit down.
opt.right.say.1 [d536ed] = 三个随口的问题，其中一个关于仲冬舞会，你就有了答案：一提到{a}的名字，{b}的脸就微微泛红。你回去汇报。{a}不得不坐下来。
# en: You are not as subtle as you think. "Is this about {a}?" says {b}, and the whole table turns round to look.
opt.right.say.2 [37ccc7] = 你没有自己以为的那么不动声色。“这是为了{a}吧？”{b}说，整张桌子的人都转过头来看。

@event between_setup_supper
# en: The Long Supper
title [9550a9] = 漫长的晚饭
# en: It was your idea that {a} and {b} share the little table by the window at supper. Twenty minutes in they have covered the weather, the soup, and the weather again. {a} keeps looking at you across the hall like someone going under for the third time.
text [5dbf84] = 让{a}和{b}在晚饭时共坐窗边那张小桌，是你的主意。二十分钟过去，他们聊了天气、汤，又聊了一遍天气。{a}隔着大厅不停地看你，像个第三次沉下水的人。
# en: Two students at a small refectory table being very polite over their soup, a third watching anxiously from across the hall.
scene [580e8e] = 膳堂里一张小桌旁，两个学生对着汤客客气气；第三个人在大厅另一头焦急地望着。
# en: Go over and rescue it
opt.left.label [969cf4] = 过去救场
# en: You sit down for five minutes and tell the story about the goat and the Lumen Ledger. Somewhere in the middle they start finishing it for you. You leave, and neither of them notices.
opt.left.say.1 [b88dbf] = 你坐过去五分钟，讲了那个关于山羊和《流明纪事报》的故事。讲到一半，他们开始替你往下讲。你起身离开，两人谁都没注意到。
# en: You sit down and the silence grows to fit three people. {b} remembers an essay. {a} thanks you for trying, in the voice of someone who wishes you hadn't.
opt.left.say.2 [0bd5e2] = 你一坐下，沉默就扩大到能装下三个人。{b}想起了一篇论文。{a}谢谢你的好意，语气却像是希望你没来过。
# en: Let it run its course
opt.right.label [0407c9] = 顺其自然
# en: You eat your own supper in peace. By pudding they've found something, possibly cheese, to disagree about cheerfully. It goes on past the candles.
opt.right.say.1 [f68627] = 你安安静静吃完自己的晚饭。到上布丁时，他们已经找到了某样可以开心争论的东西——大概是奶酪。这一聊，聊到了蜡烛燃尽之后。
# en: You eat your own supper in peace. They part at the door with a handshake, which is the saddest thing you have seen all term.
opt.right.say.2 [0d65ef] = 你安安静静吃完自己的晚饭。他们在门口握手道别，这是你整个学期见过的最让人心酸的一幕。

@event between_match_made
# en: Going Well
title [56dfbf] = 进展顺利
# en: {npc} finds you {~after class|on the stairs|at breakfast} with the look of someone who has news and has decided you're owed it first. It's going well, with the one you nudged {them} towards. Better than well. "And it was you, so. Thank you. Don't tell anyone it was you."
text [a4e063] = {npc}{~下课后|在楼梯上|早饭时}找到你，那神情像是有了消息，而且觉得该第一个告诉你。和你撮合的那个人，进展得很顺利。比顺利还要好。“这都是因为你，所以……谢谢你。别告诉别人是你撮合的。”
# en: A student grinning at a friend on a staircase, trying and failing to look casual about it.
scene [c51b95] = 楼梯上，一个学生冲朋友咧嘴笑着，想装作若无其事，却没装成。
# en: Tell just a few people
opt.left.label [be1878] = 只告诉几个人
# en: You tell exactly two people. By the end of the week you are the castle's matchmaker, whether you like it or not, and {npc} has forgiven you, mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [67a3f7] = 你只告诉了两个人。到周末时，不管你愿不愿意，你都成了全城堡的红娘；而{npc}也原谅了你，基本上。
# en: "It was all you."
opt.right.label [447635] = “全是你自己的功劳。”
# en: "It really wasn't," says {npc}, but {they} look{s} pleased anyway, and stand{s} a little taller for the rest of the month.
opt.right.say.1 [e5b035] = “真不是，”{npc}说，可看上去还是很高兴，接下来一个月都挺直了腰板。

@event between_match_soured
# en: Not Going Well
title [25cbcc] = 进展不顺
# en: It's over, the thing you nudged {npc} into, and it ended badly at a dance nobody enjoyed. {npc} has decided, on reflection, that some of this is your fault.
text [63bff2] = 你撮合{npc}的那段关系结束了，结束在一场谁都不开心的舞会上，结束得很难看。{npc}想了又想，认定这里头有一部分是你的错。
# en: A student with folded arms on a cold window seat, refusing to look at the friend who has come to sit beside them.
scene [af7a25] = 一个学生抱着胳膊坐在冰冷的窗台座上，不肯看过来坐在身边的朋友。
# en: Apologise
opt.left.label [22e908] = 道歉
# en: You say sorry for the push, and mean it. {npc} sighs. "It wasn't the push. It was the part after." By the end of the evening {npc} is telling you about it, all of it, twice.
opt.left.say.1 [2e4653] = 你为那一推道歉，是真心的。{npc}叹了口气。“不怪那一推。怪的是后来那些。”到晚上结束时，{npc}已经把来龙去脉全讲给你听了，讲了两遍。
# en: "You were keen too."
opt.right.label [264e0e] = “你当时也很上心。”
# en: It's true, and {npc} knows it, and that doesn't help at all. {They} leave{s} you with the window seat. It comes back round in a week or two; it isn't quick.
opt.right.say.1 [3f4b89] = 这是实话，{npc}也知道，可这一点用都没有。{they}把窗台座留给了你。过一两个星期就会缓过来；不会太快。

@event between_matchmaker
# en: Ask the Matchmaker
title [74e8e8] = 找红娘
# en: {~{a} corners you after class. There's someone in the year below, and {a} has heard you're the person to ask.|There's a note under your door, from {a}: "I hear you do introductions."|{a} sits down next to you at lunch with a list. It is a list of names. {a} would like your opinion on all of them.}
text [4b8ae8] = {~{a}下课后堵住了你。低年级有个人，{a}听说找你准没错。|你门缝底下有张{a}写的纸条：“听说你负责牵线。”|{a}午饭时在你身边坐下，手里拿着一张单子。是一张名单。{a}想听听你对每个人的看法。}
# en: A student sitting down opposite a friend at a library table with a folded list of names, looking hopeful.
scene [42a9f4] = 图书馆的桌边，一个学生拿着一张折好的名单在朋友对面坐下，满怀期待。
# en: Take the case
opt.left.label [e5e36f] = 接下这桩活
# en: {~You spend an evening on it, and arrange a chance meeting by the owlery that goes off almost by chance. {a} owes you a cake.|You write back: Thursday, the library, the second window. You'll never know if it worked, but {a} smiles at you in corridors now.|You go through the list, crossing out, with commentary. {a} laughs so much that the list ends up being beside the point.}
opt.left.say.1 [f7298f] = {~你花了一个晚上安排了一场在猫头鹰棚旁的“偶遇”，结果几乎真成了偶遇。{a}欠你一块蛋糕。|你回信写道：星期四，图书馆，第二扇窗。你永远不会知道成没成，但{a}现在在走廊里会冲你笑。|你逐个过名单，边划边点评。{a}笑得前仰后合，名单本身倒成了次要的。}
# en: "I'm retired."
opt.right.label [8247c9] = “我已经退休了。”
# en: {~"Retired," says {a}, unconvinced. "From what, one success?" You keep your evening.|You write "retired" under the note and slip it back. You have your evening to yourself, and you spend it, contentedly, on nobody's love life.|{a} folds the list away with great dignity. You eat your lunch in peace, and you are, you notice, a little sorry.}
opt.right.say.1 [30bd70] = {~“退休？”{a}不信。“就凭一次成功？”你保住了自己的晚上。|你在纸条下面写上“已退休”，塞了回去。你独享了一个晚上，心满意足，没为任何人的感情操心。|{a}庄重地把名单收了起来。你安安静静吃完午饭，却发现自己有点遗憾。}

@event between_likes_your_suitor
# en: Of All People
title [b05a9a] = 偏偏是他们
# en: {a} has something to confess, and takes a long time getting there. "It's {b}," {a} says at last. "I think I like {b.them}. Is that stupid?" It isn't stupid. It is complicated, because {b} has spent the last month looking for you in every room.
text [b05882] = {a}有话要坦白，绕了好久才说到正题。“是{b}，”{a}终于说，“我觉得我喜欢{b.them}。这是不是很傻？”这不傻。只是很复杂，因为过去一个月，{b}走进每个房间都在找你。
# en: Two friends on a window seat, one confiding with a hand over their face, the other going very still.
scene [508f62] = 窗台座上，一个朋友捂着脸倾诉，另一个人一下子僵住了。
# en: Tell {a} the truth
opt.left.label [98ccef] = 告诉{a}实情
# en: {a} laughs, not very happily. "Of course. Of course it's you." You stay on the window seat until {a} can say "thank you for telling me" and mean it, which takes most of the evening.
opt.left.say.1 [5160e5] = {a}笑了，笑得不怎么开心。“当然。当然是你。”你在窗台座上一直陪着，直到{a}能真心说出“谢谢你告诉我”，这几乎花了一整晚。
# en: Step back for {a}
opt.right.label [a73b0e] = 为{a}退一步
# en: You're a little cooler with {b} after that, and {b} notices, and drifts. {a} starts turning up wherever {b} is. You find you don't mind as much as you thought you would.
opt.right.say.1 [2893f5] = 那之后你对{b}冷淡了一些，{b}察觉到了，渐渐走远。{a}开始出现在{b}出现的每个地方。你发现自己并没有想象中那么在意。

@event between_partner_meets_ex
# en: The Same Fire
title [68103a] = 同一炉火
# en: The common room has a fire, a kettle and, tonight, both {a} and {b}. Your partner and your ex. They have never properly met. By the look on {b}'s face, that is about to change.
text [f8877b] = 公共休息室里有炉火，有水壶，今晚还有{a}和{b}。你的恋人，和你的前任。他们从没正式见过面。看{b}的表情，这马上就要改变了。
# en: A common room in the evening, two people on opposite sides of the fire turning at the same moment to look at a third coming through the door.
scene [15e272] = 傍晚的公共休息室，炉火两侧的两个人同时转头，看向刚进门的第三个人。
# en: Introduce them properly
opt.left.label [bcff05] = 正式介绍他们认识
# en: You make the introductions as if they were the most ordinary thing in the world. By the second cup they've found common ground: you, and a shared low opinion of your singing.
opt.left.say.1 [53f2e1] = 你介绍得仿佛这是世上最平常的事。到第二杯茶时，他们找到了共同话题：你，以及对你唱歌水平同样不高的评价。
# en: It is very polite and extremely short. Later, walking back, {a} asks one careful question, and then another, and you answer them both.
opt.left.say.2 [3c080a] = 场面非常客气，也极其短暂。后来走回去的路上，{a}问了一个小心翼翼的问题，接着又问了一个，你都答了。
# en: Steer {a} away first
opt.right.label [dbbf5b] = 先把{a}引开
# en: You invent an urgent errand and {a} lets you, which is generous. {b} watches you both go. You feel it on the back of your neck all the way up the stairs.
opt.right.say.1 [ffa76e] = 你编了个急事，{a}也由着你，这很大度。{b}看着你们俩离开。一路上楼，你都觉得后颈发烫。

@event between_admirer_gift
# en: In Front of Everyone
title [fa9f47] = 众目睽睽
# en: {~{b} turns up with a little bunch of something from the greenhouses, for you, in front of {a}.|{b} has made you a bookmark, painstakingly, and gives it to you at lunch, while {a} is sitting right there.|{b} has brought you a pastry back from the village. One pastry. {a}'s eyebrows say a great deal.}
text [923ede] = {~{b}拿着一小束温室里摘的什么花来送你，当着{a}的面。|{b}费了好大功夫给你做了个书签，午饭时送给你，而{a}就坐在旁边。|{b}从山下小镇给你带回一个酥饼。就一个。{a}的眉毛说明了一切。}
# en: A student holding out a small wrapped gift across a refectory table while the person beside its recipient raises an eyebrow.
scene [76cd8d] = 膳堂的桌边，一个学生隔着桌子递出一件包好的小礼物，收礼人身旁的人挑起了眉毛。
# en: Thank {b} warmly
opt.left.label [7f524b] = 热情地谢谢{b}
# en: {~You thank {b} and put the flowers in water. {a} is very interested in the window for the rest of the meal.|You use the bookmark that afternoon. {a} doesn't say anything about it, twice.|You eat the pastry. It is excellent. {a} watches you eat it, and the silence afterwards is long.}
opt.left.say.1 [9e5822] = {~你谢过{b}，把花插进了水里。这顿饭剩下的时间，{a}对窗外格外感兴趣。|你当天下午就用上了那个书签。{a}什么都没说，说了两次。|你把酥饼吃了。非常好吃。{a}看着你吃完，之后的沉默很长。}
# en: Hand it back, kindly
opt.right.label [9d258d] = 委婉地还回去
# en: {~"They're lovely, but I can't." {b} takes them back, pink, and leaves quickly. {a} squeezes your hand under the table.|You give the bookmark back. {b} nods, too fast. {a} doesn't gloat, which you love {them} a little more for.|You push the pastry gently back across the table. {b} eats it {b.them}self, defiantly. {a} hides a smile.}
opt.right.say.1 [514795] = {~“很漂亮，可我不能收。”{b}红着脸收回花，匆匆走了。{a}在桌下捏了捏你的手。|你把书签还了回去。{b}点头点得太快。{a}没有得意，你因此更爱{them}一点。|你把酥饼轻轻推回桌子那头。{b}赌气似的自己吃了。{a}忍住了笑。}

@event between_suitors_compare
# en: Comparing Notes
title [96ff6a] = 交流心得
# en: You come round the corner and find {a} and {b}, your two most persistent admirers, sitting together on the stairs with their heads together. Comparing notes. About you. "Oh," says {b}. "We were just..." "Comparing," says {a}.
text [db068b] = 你一转过拐角，就看见{a}和{b}——你最执着的两位追求者——并排坐在楼梯上，头凑在一起。在交流心得。关于你的。“哦，”{b}说，“我们只是……”“在交流，”{a}说。
# en: Two students sitting side by side on a staircase, heads together over a list, both looking up guiltily at a third coming round the corner.
scene [01760d] = 两个学生并排坐在楼梯上，头凑在一张单子上，一起心虚地抬头看向从拐角走来的第三个人。
# en: Sit down and join in
opt.left.label [6f9b9f] = 坐下一起聊
# en: You sit on the step below and dispute every point. By the end all three of you are laughing, they've agreed you're impossible, and nobody has to choose anything today.
opt.left.say.1 [702999] = 你在下一级台阶坐下，对每一条都提出异议。到最后，三个人都笑了，他们一致认定你不可理喻，今天谁也不用做选择。
# en: You try to be funny about it and it comes out defensive. They exchange a look that you are not part of. That's new.
opt.left.say.2 [5383ec] = 你想说得幽默些，出口却像在辩解。他们交换了一个你不在其中的眼神。这倒是头一回。
# en: Walk on with dignity
opt.right.label [a570cd] = 体面地走开
# en: You step over them and carry on down the stairs. Behind you, the comparing resumes, louder, and someone says "the hair, though", and they both laugh.
opt.right.say.1 [4636ed] = 你从他们身边跨过去，继续下楼。身后的交流又开始了，声音更大，有人说“不过那头发啊”，两人都笑了。

@event between_secret_about
# en: Not Mine to Tell
title [8af199] = 轮不到我说
# en: "You can't tell anyone," says {a}, and then tells you anyway: {b} failed last term's practical, and has been resitting it in secret every week, and is terrified of anyone finding out. {a} looks relieved to have put it down. Now you're holding it.
text [2bbb16] = “你不能告诉任何人，”{a}说，然后还是告诉了你：{b}上学期的实践课没过，每个星期都在偷偷补考，生怕被人知道。{a}看上去像是终于卸下了担子。现在担子在你手里了。
# en: A student leaning close to whisper to a friend in a corridor, a third student visible at the far end, unaware.
scene [103bbe] = 走廊里，一个学生凑近朋友耳语，走廊尽头隐约可见第三个毫不知情的学生。
# en: Tell {a} it wasn't {a.theirs} to tell
opt.left.label [c25eb2] = 告诉{a}这轮不到{a.them}说
# en: {a} flushes. "I only told you." You point out that this is what everyone says. {a} doesn't speak to you until supper, and is quieter about other people afterwards.
opt.left.say.1 [375a5d] = {a}脸红了。“我只告诉了你。”你指出，大家都是这么说的。直到晚饭前{a}都没跟你说话，之后谈论别人时也安静了许多。
# en: Keep it, and help {b} quietly
opt.right.label [d0b5f2] = 守住秘密，悄悄帮{b}
# en: You start turning up where {b} revises, with your notes, as if by accident. {b} doesn't ask why. The practical gets easier, for both of you.
opt.right.say.1 [9402d8] = 你开始“碰巧”带着笔记出现在{b}复习的地方。{b}没问为什么。那门实践课变得容易了些，对你们俩都是。

@event between_did_they_tell
# en: Somebody Told You
title [da8bcd] = 有人告诉你了
# en: {npc} sits down across from you with the face of someone who has rehearsed this. "Somebody told you. About the practical. Didn't they?"
text [5831f9] = {npc}在你对面坐下，一副排练过的样子。“有人告诉你了。实践课的事。对不对？”
# en: A student sitting down across a library table from a friend, hands flat on the wood, clearly having rehearsed something.
scene [56a191] = 图书馆的桌边，一个学生在朋友对面坐下，双手平放在桌上，显然事先想好了要说什么。
# en: Tell the truth
opt.left.label [d8bf00] = 说实话
# en: {npc} nods slowly. "I thought so. Thank you for not pretending." {npc} doesn't ask who. You suspect {they} know{s}.
opt.left.say.1 [3c9d0b] = {npc}慢慢点了点头。“我就知道。谢谢你没有装傻。”{npc}没问是谁。你猜{they}心里有数。
# en: "Nobody told me anything."
opt.right.label [9880ab] = “没人跟我说过什么。”
# en: {npc} lets out a breath held for a month. "Good. Good. Sorry. I've been seeing it in everyone's face." You change the subject, and {they} let{s} you.
opt.right.say.1 [b8cf0b] = {npc}长出了一口憋了一个月的气。“那就好。好。抱歉。我总觉得在每个人脸上都看到了。”你转开了话题，{they}也由着你。
# en: {npc} doesn't believe a word, and now there are two people {they} can't quite trust. {They} pick{s} up {their} books and leave{s}.
opt.right.say.2 [f0dcd0] = {npc}一个字都不信，现在{they}又多了一个不太能信任的人。{they}收起书走了。

@event between_rumour_from_you
# en: How It Grew
title [5ca387] = 越传越大
# en: {~You mentioned, once, in passing, that {a} had lent {b} a scarf. By supper they're engaged.|You said {a} and {b} were revising together. By morning it's a secret romance, with details.|You told one person that {a} walked {b} back from the library. The story has since acquired a moonlit lake.} Both of them have heard it. Both of them know where it started.
text [371e56] = {~你曾随口提过一句，{a}借了条围巾给{b}。到晚饭时，他们已经订婚了。|你说过{a}和{b}在一起复习。到第二天早上，就成了一段秘密恋情，还有细节。|你只跟一个人说过，{a}从图书馆送{b}回来。这个故事后来添上了一片月光下的湖。}两人都听说了。两人都知道是从哪儿传出来的。
# en: A cluster of students whispering behind their hands in a corridor, two others at opposite ends of it pointedly not looking at each other.
scene [f3bbe6] = 走廊里一群学生捂着嘴窃窃私语，走廊两头的两个人刻意不看对方。
# en: Set the record straight
opt.left.label [07105d] = 澄清事实
# en: {~You spend a day explaining that a scarf is only a scarf. Half the castle is disappointed in you. {a} and {b} are not.|You correct it at every table, which makes it sound truer. {b} thanks you anyway.|You say it was a library, and a corridor, and no lake. People believe you, sadly. {a} buys you a cider.}
opt.left.say.1 [0cac56] = {~你花了一整天解释，一条围巾只是一条围巾。半个城堡都对你很失望。{a}和{b}没有。|你在每张桌边纠正，结果越纠正越像真的。{b}还是谢了你。|你说只有图书馆和走廊，没有湖。大家信了，有点遗憾。{a}请你喝了杯苹果酒。}
# en: Let it run
opt.right.label [cf7c46] = 由它去传
# en: {~It's quite funny, the first week. {a} doesn't find it funny at all. {b} starts wearing the scarf.|The details get better. {a} stops sitting with you. {b} seems, oddly, not to mind.|By the end of the month nobody can remember whether it was true, including, it seems, {a} and {b}.}
opt.right.say.1 [856604] = {~头一个星期还挺好笑。{a}一点都不觉得好笑。{b}开始围那条围巾了。|细节越编越精彩。{a}不再跟你坐一起了。{b}倒是出奇地不在意。|到月底，谁也记不清那是不是真的了，似乎连{a}和{b}自己也记不清了。}

@event between_overheard
# en: Behind Their Back
title [b15768] = 背后议论
# en: {~Behind the library shelves, {a} is telling a little group exactly what {a.they} think{a.s} of {b}. It isn't kind, and it isn't true.|On the stairs, {a} is doing an impression of {b}. It's a good impression. People are laughing.|{a} is holding court at the refectory table: {b}'s spells, {b}'s family, {b}'s hair.} {b} is a friend of yours, and isn't here.
text [5a28a8] = {~图书馆书架后面，{a}正对着一小群人细数{a.they}对{b}的看法。既不厚道，也不属实。|楼梯上，{a}在模仿{b}。模仿得很像。大家都在笑。|{a}在膳堂的桌边高谈阔论：{b}的咒语，{b}的家人，{b}的头发。}{b}是你的朋友，而{b.they}不在场。
# en: A student holding court at a refectory table, mid-impression, the others laughing, a fourth student behind them stopping still with a tray.
scene [b14eb0] = 膳堂的桌边，一个学生正模仿别人模仿到一半，旁人哄笑，身后第四个端着餐盘的学生停住了脚步。
# en: Speak up
opt.left.label [a3103e] = 站出来说话
# en: {~"That isn't true, and you know it." The group goes quiet. {a} looks at you as if you've changed sides in a war you didn't know about. Word gets back to {b}, eventually.|"Do me next," you say. Nobody laughs. {a} stops. It gets back to {b} by the end of the week.|You put your tray down at the table and say {b}'s name kindly, once, and leave it there. {a} finds someone else to talk about.}
opt.left.say.1 [f623ea] = {~“这不是真的，你自己也知道。”那群人安静了下来。{a}看着你，仿佛你在一场你都不知道的战争里倒戈了。这话最终还是传到了{b}耳朵里。|“下一个学我吧，”你说。没人笑。{a}停了下来。不到周末，这事就传到了{b}那里。|你把餐盘放到那张桌上，和气地提了一次{b}的名字，就此打住。{a}换了个人议论。}
# en: Say nothing
opt.right.label [d1151d] = 一言不发
# en: {~You keep walking. The laughing follows you down the aisle. You sit with {b} at supper and don't mention it, and it sits between you.|You laugh, a little, because everyone is. You think about it for the rest of the day.|You eat your lunch somewhere else. It doesn't help as much as you'd like.}
opt.right.say.1 [bb50d6] = {~你继续往前走。笑声一路跟着你。晚饭时你和{b}坐在一起，没提这事，它就横在你们之间。|你也笑了一点，因为大家都在笑。这件事你想了一整天。|你去别处吃了午饭。这并没有你希望的那么管用。}

@event between_betting_book
# en: The Book on Them
title [27e044] = 押在他们身上
# en: There's a book running in the common room, and the odds are on {a} and {b}: together by the end of term, three to one. Somebody you don't much like is taking the money. Everyone is very interested in what you know.
text [d6b253] = 公共休息室里有人开了赌盘，押的是{a}和{b}：学期结束前在一起，三赔一。收钱的是个你不太喜欢的人。大家都很想知道你知道些什么。
# en: A grubby ledger open on a common-room table, students crowding round to write names and coins in its columns.
scene [d9c63d] = 公共休息室的桌上摊着一本脏兮兮的账簿，学生们围过去，在栏目里写下名字和钱数。
# en: Put a crown on them
opt.left.label [d0c53f] = 押一克朗
# en: You put your crown on "together". Three weeks later they are, and you collect. You never tell either of them, and you feel slightly odd every time they hold hands.
opt.left.say.1 [7b903f] = 你把一克朗押在“在一起”上。三个星期后，他们真的在一起了，你收了钱。你从没告诉过他们俩，每次看见他们牵手，你都觉得有点怪。
# en: You put your crown on "together", and they aren't, quite, and the bookmaker smiles at you every morning for a month.
opt.left.say.2 [5c41c9] = 你把一克朗押在“在一起”上，可他们终究没能走到那一步，接下来一个月，那个庄家每天早上都冲你笑。
# en: Shut the book down
opt.right.label [447c4f] = 把赌盘掀了
# en: You take the ledger and drop it in the fire, which is not a popular move. The bookmaker sulks. {a} and {b} never find out about it, or if they do they never say.
opt.right.say.1 [8bba8e] = 你拿起账簿扔进了炉火，这一举动很不受欢迎。庄家生起了闷气。{a}和{b}始终不知道这件事，就算知道，也从没提过。

@event between_couple_bubble
# en: Party of Two
title [f6b4e2] = 两人世界
# en: {~{a} and {b} have become inseparable, and now they finish each other's sentences, and you finish your supper.|You've been the third chair at {a} and {b}'s table for a month now. Tonight they forgot to pull it out.|{a} and {b} save you a place on the window seat. When you get there, it's a seat for two and a cushion for you.}
text [e219dd] = {~{a}和{b}变得形影不离，如今他们能接上彼此的话，而你只能接着吃完自己的晚饭。|你在{a}和{b}的桌边当了一个月的第三把椅子。今晚，他们忘了给你拉开它。|{a}和{b}在窗边座位上给你留了个位置。你到了才发现，是两人份的座位，外加给你的一个坐垫。}
# en: Two students sharing one cushion on a window seat, a third sitting slightly apart with a sandwich.
scene [20d15f] = 窗边座位上，两个学生共用一个坐垫，第三个人拿着三明治坐得稍远。
# en: Say something
opt.left.label [fac1f4] = 说出来
# en: {~"I'm still here, you know." They look at you, horrified, and then they laugh, and the next evening there are three cups.|It comes out more plaintive than you meant. {b} hugs you. {a} saves your chair for a week, pointedly.|You mention the cushion. {a} apologises for some time. It's awkward, and then it's better.}
opt.left.say.1 [1259a2] = {~“我还在这儿呢。”他们惊恐地看着你，然后笑了，第二天晚上桌上就有了三个杯子。|说出口比你想的要可怜巴巴。{b}抱了抱你。{a}特意给你留了一个星期的椅子。|你提起了那个坐垫。{a}道歉道了好半天。场面先是尴尬，然后就好了。}
# en: Give them room
opt.right.label [645df9] = 给他们留点空间
# en: {~You eat early and read late. You've never got so much done. You miss them.|You leave them to it. Your essays improve. Your evenings don't.|You find other company for a while. They come back round, eventually, the way people do.}
opt.right.say.1 [843292] = {~你早早吃饭，晚晚看书。你从没这么高效过。你想念他们。|你随他们去了。你的论文进步了。你的晚上没有。|你找了别的伙伴待了一阵子。他们最终会回来的，人总是这样。}
